{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20339",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 4.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.93,
      "end_seconds": 9.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.23,
      "end_seconds": 15.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "It's some chest discomfort when I climb stairs, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.61,
      "end_seconds": 20.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.11,
      "end_seconds": 37.56,
      "duration_seconds": 15.45,
      "text": "It's, It's been going on for about a year. I just want to get back to normal, really. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.47,
      "end_seconds": 42.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Right, how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.19,
      "end_seconds": 55.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "I'd give it a three, out of ten. I did have bruising easily at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.01,
      "end_seconds": 59.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.21,
      "end_seconds": 73.97,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for about a year. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. Diabetes, for nearly five years. I've, I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.67,
      "end_seconds": 82.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.27,
      "end_seconds": 85.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.26,
      "end_seconds": 99.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.23,
      "end_seconds": 106.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "I mean, you know, I had my tonsils removed as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.52,
      "end_seconds": 111.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.91,
      "end_seconds": 131.06,
      "duration_seconds": 18.15,
      "text": "I take atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol. Let me think, it's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.93,
      "end_seconds": 154.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.13,
      "end_seconds": 158.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Right, my grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.85,
      "end_seconds": 162.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Alright, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.55,
      "end_seconds": 167.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.89,
      "end_seconds": 169.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.74,
      "end_seconds": 175.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.42,
      "end_seconds": 178.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Has there been any fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.19,
      "end_seconds": 180.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Definitely no fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.33,
      "end_seconds": 191.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "A few quick ones: pain at rest, palpitations or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.73,
      "end_seconds": 199.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.57,
      "end_seconds": 202.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.39,
      "end_seconds": 206.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Erm, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.06,
      "end_seconds": 211.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.59,
      "end_seconds": 214.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.1,
      "end_seconds": 219.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.84,
      "end_seconds": 235.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.39,
      "end_seconds": 262.72,
      "duration_seconds": 15.33,
      "text": "Okay: weight 55 kilos, BP is 126 over 72, respiratory rate 17, pulse is 85 beats a minute, BMI works out to 23.8, height 152 centimetres, temperature is 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.74,
      "end_seconds": 267.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Mm, um, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.06,
      "end_seconds": 273.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.44,
      "end_seconds": 279.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.0,
      "end_seconds": 283.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.39,
      "end_seconds": 305.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.31,
      "end_seconds": 312.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.09,
      "end_seconds": 349.7,
      "duration_seconds": 19.61,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding. I want blood tests done, that's for bruising and bleeding. The treatment will be pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. It's for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.93,
      "end_seconds": 352.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.68,
      "end_seconds": 360.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.44,
      "end_seconds": 366.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Can you send me for a lipid profile?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.47,
      "end_seconds": 388.23,
      "duration_seconds": 20.76,
      "text": "I don't think that's needed at this stage, the history doesn't call for it. If you pass black stools or have prolonged bleeding, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Let's review you after the blood results. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.97,
      "end_seconds": 392.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}